From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ElXreno <elxreno@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:53:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: hda/realtek: Initialize ALC1316 amps on MSI Titan 18 HX
 A2W

The MSI Titan 18 HX A2W (codec SSID 1462:1500) routes all speakers
through two Realtek ALC1316 smart amps at I2C addresses 0x10 and 0x12,
reached over the ALC274 COEF bridge the same way as the ALC1318 on
ThinkPads. Linux never programs them, so the speakers play in the
amps' power-on state without the vendor tuning.

Replay the register sequence the Windows driver writes at load time,
taken from a VFIO trace of the HDA controller: COEF 0x10 bit 15 is
set, bit 14 is cleared around amp access, then 88 writes per amp
including the per-amp biquads. Power the amps up on PCM open and down
on close as the Windows driver does, and reprogram them on S3/S4
resume.

The trace ends with the gain from the 1B48/2B48 blocks of the vendor
profile (0xc012/0xc013 = 0xef). Program the 1A48/2A48 value 0xf7
instead, which the same profile holds for both amps and which measures
3 dB louder.
